  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as in step 1; nothing was added or dropped.",
   "Pi header pins use the catalogue's physical pin numbers. GND is pin 9 and GPIO17 is pin 11, matching the highlighted GND and GP17 labels in the image.",
   "The buzzer's negative leg (pin 1) is in column 15 and goes through the black wire to GND. Its positive leg (pin 2) is in column 18 and goes through the purple wire to GPIO17, as the buzzer card requires.",
   "The breadboard rows are an assumption. The image does not show the leg and wire holes separately, so I put the buzzer legs in row b and the wire ends in row a of the same columns (15 and 18). Rows a-e are bank 't' in the catalogue's naming.",
   "The wires are modelled as male-to-female: the male end goes into the breadboard and the female end onto the Pi header pin.",
   "No resistor is used, since the tutorial and image show none."
  ]
 },
